  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Light showers gradually dissipate through the\nevening. \n\nLight showers across the region this afternoon will gradually\ndissipate this evening as a weak low moves offshore. Clouds and\nperhaps some patchy fog or drizzle may linger overnight before \nhigh pressure builds in from the west, bringing in drier\nconditions by Monday morning. Overnight lows will fall into the \n50s.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Tranquil weather expected this week with no \nsignificant weather hazards anticipated. \n\nHigh pressure will be in control through much of the week resulting \nin mostly clear skies and comfortable temperatures. We will feel a \nbit of an early Fall chill with a cold front passing late Monday \nthough. Highs on Tuesday only get into the low to mid 60s with \novernight lows on Tuesday Night/Wednesday morning dropping into the \nupper 30s and low to mid 40s. Even with the early Fall chill, \ntemperatures should remain high enough to not need any frost \nheadlines just yet. Cannot rule out some temperatures in the mid 30s \nthough in the Poconos. \n\nTemperatures return to more seasonable levels on Wednesday and \nlikely go into the above normal range towards the end of the week as \nit should be a pleasant stretch of days.",
